-      "conclusion": "The five original C releases each complete separate live- and null-interpreter processes with 145 raw primitive rows per route; current Jim completes 108 live primitive rows and 37 explicit API-unavailable rows in its successfully linked image. Every primitive error leaves all four output sentinels unchanged in these exact rows. All measured native ABIs report 4-byte int, 8-byte long/wide/double/pointer and CHAR_BIT=8. Tcl_UniChar is 2 bytes for C8 and 4 for C9; probe translation-unit width macros and retained library configuration remain separate. C Int converts String 2147483648 to raw -2147483648 but rejects 4294967296. LP64 Long accepts 9223372036854775808 as -9223372036854775808 and 18446744073709551615 as -1 on all five C releases. C8 Wide accepts those same positive values; C9 Wide rejects both with unchanged sentinel. C8 Long accepts the measured negative beyond-signed-width inputs with wrapped results, while C9 rejects them. String NaN Double succeeds on C8.4/current Jim but fails on C8.5/C8.6/C9, with release-specific cache/result/error metadata. A cached Jim integer 17 produces raw Boolean 17 with no string materialisation; cached 4294967296 produces raw Boolean 0. Fresh Jim String 17 instead fails Boolean parsing. C cached integer Boolean outputs are 1 in those controls, with C8.4 boolean/string conversion distinguished from later cached integer routes. Every C null-interpreter row preserves the separately seeded result and observable errorCode, although selected live error formatting can change string residency. Jim primitive errors preserve seeded public errorCode while publishing the exact diagnostic result. Complete raw rows retain every constructor/getter/code/errno/primary/string/output/result/error observation independently; they are not normalized into expression truth. Current marked source definitions compare selected raw primitive fields and independently exercise target availability, actual host stages, original-cache transport and failure-rendering obligations. Jim cached Boolean returns its raw C integer; expression/command truth remains a separate purpose. Supported descriptive target fields are exactly CHAR_BIT=8, int=4 and long=8. C84 fresh numeric Boolean narrows reached signed long to C int before truth, while cachedWide truth stays independent. Retained original library TCL_DEFS includes TCL_WIDE_INT_IS_LONG=1 independently of the probe translation unit BUILD_MACRO0. The public software scalar facade requires an independently issued per-object engine/Host/ABI/runtime/epoch context. Null access has no fallback issuer; weak receipts neither retain a retired object nor keep its interpreter alive. Change-and-restore cannot revive a stale issuer. Native public rows describe primitive observations only and do not grant this application ownership. Direct C84 invalid-input primitive errors retain the existing errorCode for all five public getter kinds. An additional propagation receipt describes the later NONE update and is consumed only by the actual Runtime log or VM evaluated completion boundary. Explicit Long overflow remains independently scoped. The current Long-octal control compares nine bounded original live08 windows without borrowing the Double/Boolean invalid-octal purpose for a modern integer-only Long failure. Two separately selected C9 Long success value/cache windows remain distinct. Boxed primitive reads retain their actually queried numeric environment and original engine issuer; raw Boolean getter integers remain separate from semantic truth. Missing or changed-and-restored issuer/ABI refuses before output and later cache effects. The entered ValueOps primitive source control preserves selected cache, raw Boolean projection, prior result and original rc0/reference roles under the actual software issuer; it adds no external primitive or expression-truth observation.",
