te or executed Rust consumer assertion follows. These are source/API bindings with no attached assertion outcome or inferred executable availability. Pure comparisons cover two Jim cached Boolean rows, 140 selected CLong rows, selected C90Long/Wide edges,58 C84Boolean value/cache rows and four C85+BooleanNaN live diagnostic/String windows. Actual host controls separately compare six freshJimLong errno rows and 44 selected freshC84Boolean errno rows; explicit harness resets reproduce the original request and are not getter effects. Synthetic unsupported layouts, deliberate prior ERANGE, negative 17 transport, custom NaN payloads and counted 17NULX geometry are software controls, not additional original captures. int/wideInt cache names normalize to the software integer class in the pure Long comparison; no physical native primary/header identity follows. Targetless numeric refusal does not imply source evaluation failure. Existing 1558 raw rows, 37 Jim API-unavailable rows and original failedJim compile/successful unchanged linked458 retry remain immutable. No generic counted-NUL numeric acceptance, ExprBool/NOT/conditional/logical-site equivalence, wasm32/LLP64/BIGIP/application ABI issuer, native handler/lifetime/frame or cache/result authority is inferred. These thirteen current source controls attach no assertion outcome or executable admission. The bounded comparison covers 300 C rows and two cached Jim Boolean rows; it compares selected public outputs/cache class/String correspondence/result/errorCode, not original private header or app-issued receipt identity. Constructed null sentinel, weak lifetime, duplicate/replacement, epoch, foreign Host, no-numeric-ABI and first-cause controls are software invariants. Native456 initial failed Jim linkage and successful unchanged458 capture remain independent and immutable. No expression/NOT/condition/logical-site equivalence, external callback chronology, source entry/frame, output ABI default, current store or arbitrary setter authority is inferred. The three current controls are unexecuted. Native comparisons are bounded to five direct original456 code/result/errorCode fields and three older independently captured Wide/Double/Boolean callback-Eval message/errorCode fields, plus the selected Long overflow code. Int/Long propagation is a software/source recipe obligation rather than an additional original process observation. Default Runtime and actual selected VM fixture publication controls grant no Native error flags, external header/result identity, scalar issuer, application admission, every error origin or expression truth parity. Original provider answers/evidence/replay and the failed independent Syntax301/302 Long comparisons remain unchanged. This added source definition is unexecuted. Its Native field comparisons are limited to seven selected live failure code/message/errorCode/no-cache observations and two C9 Long live success value/cache-kind observations from the unchanged original456 capture. Original140 live/null comparisons, earlier1113/390 comparisons and failed Syntax301/302 assertions retain their own scope; no completed whole comparison, private object/header identity, application issuer, new ABI width, other counted/NUL bytes or expression-truth permission is inferred. Source303 predates this control. The added scalar ABI source controls issue no new external getter observation, C ABI width certificate, original header or expression-truth result. Their actual Runtime target requires its own successful producer, inventory and assertion receipt; the separate failed Runtime311 build supplies none. Current direct test attributes and real module parents attach these source/API contracts only. They do not certify an executable inventory, passed assertion, complete Native comparison or changed-current-image result. Each original provider answer and independently closed software command retains its exact input/channel/source purpose.",
