+      "conclusion": "A positioned Logical source projection retains complete original words, the positively validated full editing input and the same ContextRegistry. Both retained profiles must lack an actual native name protocol, and hosted inputs remain separate. A lexical core point may remain present, including the projected Jim0.79 authoring context, and grants no Native naming policy; the unversioned Tcl authored simulation is not an execution recipe for this source purpose. Authored transition lineage and genuine conditional declaration observations keep their own applicability. A bounded own Logical procedure inventory additionally retains the Registry-selected Procedure definition, original unchanged parent body geometry and each child's same-image/full-config source vector. Child mutations affect only the cloned conditional inventory and never publish parent execution facts. Unknown values remain unknown; arbitrary braces are not scripts, cooked coordinates and unsupported namespace/frame recipes decline. Native or hosted missing owners cannot enter Logical advice. Keyword shortening uses complete static ASCII controls and the selected leading option prefix, preserving reserved positional tails and values. Editing rejects prior mutation uncertainty independently of readonly source metadata. No body presence, source schema or graph hypothesis supplies runtime lookup, installed frames, Native naming, Normal completion or operand-effect closure. Analyser::selected_logical_declaration_advice selects positively retained actual Logical ResolvedAnalysisInput consistently at all five analysis entrypoints, independently excluding a captured Native entry and NativeRecipe. The plain Logical authored C8.6 name simulation can be present without Native protocol and does not disable this compatibility domain. Hosted/mixed input and missing actual retained result input cannot donate advice. Authored-name geometry supplies no formal parameter grammar: plain tcl keeps parameter_grammar unavailable until a formal dialect is independently selected. AnalysisResult::allows_lexical_declaration_advice itself requires positively retained actual Logical input and excludes hosted original source; allows_retained_logical_declaration_advice delegates to it. Copying a flag/profile/report table cannot reopen missing/Native/hosted ingress for any consumer. Original variable completion/source references return compatibility fallback only in this positive domain; malformed geometry and unavailable ownership are terminal empty source results. Workspace symbols require current complete source context before choosing original versus Logical presentation advice. Logical class calls retain their separate source consumer domain: an authentic retained Logical source_class receipt is positive for its Logical owner, while Native command_query continues to that separate owner rather than fabricate a Native class record or intercept the Logical call.",
